.TH CAPTURE-VIEW 1 "May 2026" "capture-view 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
capture-view \- low-latency HDMI USB capture-card viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B capture-view
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B capture-view
shows the newest available frame from a V4L2/UVC HDMI capture device and can monitor PipeWire audio with small buffers.
It is a real-time monitor, not a buffered media player.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --list-devices
List V4L2 video capture devices and supported formats.
.TP
.B --list-audio
List PipeWire audio source and sink nodes.
.TP
.B --doctor
Print troubleshooting information.
.TP
.B --wizard
Run interactive setup wizard and start viewer with selected settings.
.TP
.B --gtk
Open a minimal GTK launcher for selecting common viewer settings and starting the SDL viewer.
.TP
.BI --diagnostic-bundle " PATH"
Write doctor output, video modes, audio nodes, and last config to PATH.
.TP
.B --save-config
Save selected options to the active config/profile.
.TP
.BI --profile " NAME"
Use a named config profile.
.TP
.B --list-profiles
List known config profiles.
.TP
.B --init-profiles
Create default console, audio-test, and safe profiles if missing.
.TP
.BI --video " /dev/video0"
Select V4L2 video device.
.TP
.BI --video-output " /dev/videoN"
Write frames to a V4L2 output device such as v4l2loopback.
.TP
.BI --video-output-format " yuyv|nv12|rgba"
Choose V4L2 output pixel format for v4l2loopback.
.TP
.BI --size " WIDTHxHEIGHT"
Request video size.
.TP
.BI --fps " FPS"
Request frame rate.
.TP
.BI --format " auto|mjpeg|yuyv|nv12"
Request pixel format. auto tries raw formats before MJPEG.
.TP
.BI --latency-mode " ultra|low|balanced"
Apply preset buffer/vsync/audio-buffer settings.
.TP
.BI --frame-pacing " immediate|yield|sleep|adaptive"
Choose render-loop pacing. immediate never waits, yield gives the scheduler a chance after each frame, sleep targets requested FPS, adaptive sleeps then yields near the target present time.
.TP
.BI --output-scaling " fit|fill|stretch|integer"
Choose render scaling mode.
.TP
.BI --upscale-quality " nearest|bilinear|bilinear-rcas"
Choose texture filtering for enlarged video. bilinear is default. nearest is cheapest but lower quality. bilinear-rcas adds a GPU sharpening pass.
.TP
.BI --rcas-strength " 0.0..1.0"
Set RCAS sharpening strength. 0 disables sharpening, 0.35 is the recommended default, 0.75 is aggressive.
.TP
.B --borderless
Start without window decorations/titlebar for cleaner screen sharing or OBS capture.
.TP
.BI --log-file " PATH"
Append diagnostic logs to PATH while still printing logs to stderr.
.TP
.B --verbose
Enable debug-level logs.
.TP
.B --audio-monitor
Enable PipeWire input-to-output audio monitor.
.TP
.B --audio-test-tone
Generate a quiet 440 Hz tone to test the selected audio output.
.TP
.BI --audio-input " NAME_OR_ID"
Target PipeWire audio source.
.TP
.BI --audio-output " NAME_OR_ID"
Target PipeWire audio sink.
.TP
.BI --audio-virtual-source " NAME"
Create a PipeWire virtual audio source for apps such as Discord.
.TP
.BI --audio-buffer-ms " MS"
Set audio monitor buffer size.
.TP
.BI --audio-quantum " FRAMES"
Request PipeWire processing quantum. Defaults to half the audio buffer, clamped to 128-512 frames.
.TP
.B --no-audio-autotune
Disable automatic audio buffer increase after repeated underruns/overruns.
.TP
.BI --audio-delay-ms " MS"
Set audio delay adjustment from -200 to +200 ms. Negative delay requires video delay and is kept at minimum latency.
.TP
.B --test-pattern
Run generated video test pattern.
.TP
.BI --benchmark " SECONDS"
Run for a fixed time and print latency-focused render timing metrics.
.SH SHORTCUTS
F toggles fullscreen. Alt+B toggles borderless/titlebar. U cycles upscale quality. [ and ] adjust RCAS strength. V toggles vsync. S toggles stats. G toggles GUI overlay. R restarts capture. A restarts audio. M mutes audio. + and - adjust volume. O cycles scaling. Esc exits fullscreen or quits.
.SH CONFIG
Config is stored at
.I ~/.config/lowlat-capture-viewer/config.toml
unless disabled with
.B --no-config.
